<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Web Technology Notes</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #f1f5f9;
            margin: 0;
        }

        nav {
            background: #4f46e5;
            color: white;
            padding: 18px 8%;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
        }

        nav h2 {
            margin: 0;
        }

        nav a {
            color: white;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        .container {
            padding: 40px 8%;
        }

        .topic {
            background: white;
            padding: 25px;
            margin: 20px 0;
            border-radius: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
        }

        h1 {
            color: #1e293b;
        }

        h2 {
            color: #4f46e5;
        }

        p {
            color: #475569;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        code {
            background: #e2e8f0;
            padding: 4px 7px;
            border-radius: 5px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <nav>
        <h2>🌐 Web Technology Notes</h2>
        <a href="/notes">← Back to Notes</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="container">

        <h1>Web Technology 📚</h1>

        <p>
            Basic HTML, CSS and web development study materials.
        </p>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>1. HTML</h2>

            <p>
                HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language.
                It is used to create the structure of web pages.
            </p>

            <p>
                Example:
                <code>&lt;h1&gt;Hello World&lt;/h1&gt;</code>
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>2. CSS</h2>

            <p>
                CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets.
                It is used to design and style web pages.
            </p>

            <p>
                Example:
                <code>color: blue;</code>
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>3. JavaScript</h2>

            <p>
                JavaScript is a programming language used to
                add interaction and dynamic behaviour to web pages.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>4. Front-End Development</h2>

            <p>
                Front-end development focuses on the visible
                part of a website that users interact with.
            </p>

            <p>
                Common technologies are HTML, CSS and JavaScript.
            </p>
        </div>

    </div>

</body>
